"1. Let \(A\) be an \(n\times n\) real matrix. Which statements are true?","If \(0\) is an eigenvalue of \(A\), then \(A\) is non-invertible.","If \(A\) is non-invertible, then \(0\) is an eigenvalue of \(A\).","If \(A\) has a zero row, then \(0\) must be an eigenvalue of \(A\).","If \(A\) has a zero eigenvalue, then \(\det(A)=0\).","A,B,C,D","Correct: a zero eigenvalue forces \(\det(A)=0\).","Correct: non-invertible \(\Leftrightarrow \det(A)=0\).","Correct: a zero row forces rank \(<n\), so \(0\) is an eigenvalue.","Correct: product of eigenvalues equals determinant."
"2. Let \(A\) be symmetric with eigenvalues \(\lambda_1\ge\cdots\ge\lambda_n\). What is true about \(\max_{\|x\|=1} x^TAx\)?","The maximum equals \(\lambda_1\).","It is attained exactly at eigenvectors for \(\lambda_1\).","It depends on the choice of basis.","For all unit \(x,\;x^TAx\le \lambda_1\).","A,B,D","Correct: Rayleigh-Ritz theorem.","Correct: maximizers are eigenvectors for the top eigenvalue.","Incorrect: the value is basis-independent.","Correct: Rayleigh quotient never exceeds \(\lambda_1\)."
"3. Let \(A\) be symmetric with eigenpairs \((\lambda_i,v_i)\). Which statements are true about \(A^k\)?","Eigenvalues of \(A^k\) are \(\lambda_i^k\).","Every eigenvector of \(A\) is an eigenvector of \(A^k\).","Eigenvalue multiplicities are preserved for all \(k\).","\(A^k\) is diagonalizable iff \(A\) is diagonalizable.","A,B,D","Correct: follows from spectral theorem.","Correct: \(A^k v_i = \lambda_i^k v_i\).","Incorrect: powers can merge eigenvalues (e.g., \(\lambda\) and \(-\lambda\)).","Correct: powers of a diagonalizable matrix remain diagonalizable."
"4. Let \(A\) be \(m\times n\). Suppose \(\sigma^2>0\) is a nonzero eigenvalue of both \(A^TA\) and \(AA^T\). Which are true?","If \(v\) is an eigenvector of \(A^TA\) with eigenvalue \(\sigma^2\), then \(Av\) is an eigenvector of \(AA^T\) with eigenvalue \(\sigma^2\).","If \(u\) is an eigenvector of \(AA^T\) with eigenvalue \(\sigma^2\), then \(A^Tu\) is an eigenvector of \(A^TA\) with eigenvalue \(\sigma^2\).","The nonzero eigenvalues of \(A^TA\) and \(AA^T\) always coincide.","If \(v\) is an eigenvector of \(A^TA\) with eigenvalue \(\sigma^2>0\), then \(Av\neq 0\); similarly \(A^Tu\neq 0\).","A,B,C,D","Correct: follows from \(A^TAv=\sigma^2 v\).","Correct: symmetric argument via \(AA^T u=\sigma^2 u\).","Correct: nonzero spectra match (SVD theory).","Correct: positivity forces \(Av\) and \(A^Tu\) nonzero."
"5. Let \(A\) be a real symmetric matrix with decomposition \(A = V\Lambda V^T\). Which statements are true?","Columns of \(V\) can be chosen orthonormal.","\(\Lambda\) lists eigenvalues of \(A\) with multiplicity.","The decomposition is unique when eigenvalues are distinct.","For symmetric \(A\), it may happen that \(A\neq V\Lambda V^T\).","A,B,C","Correct: symmetric matrices admit orthonormal eigenbases.","Correct: diagonal entries are eigenvalues.","Correct: distinct eigenvalues fix eigenvectors up to sign.","Incorrect: for symmetric \(A\), always \(A = V\Lambda V^T\)."
